From: Alexander Schwankner <mrmoor4@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/tegra: fuse: read the platform from HIDREV on TF-A based
 SoCs

Since 8b8ee2e56f95 ("soc/tegra: Use ARM SMCCC to get chip ID, revision,
and platform info") the platform comes from bits [15:8] of the SMCCC SoC
revision. The TF-A firmware on Tegra194 and Tegra234 puts the HIDREV
major revision there ((major << 8) | minor, 0x401 on Orin), so the
kernel reports the platform as "Asim QT" and tegra_is_silicon() returns
false. On Jetson Orin the nvgpu driver then runs about 7x slower.

Read the platform from HIDREV again on Tegra210, Tegra186, Tegra194 and
Tegra234, and keep SMCCC for Tegra241 and later. Chip ID and revision
still come from SMCCC.

Fixes: 8b8ee2e56f95 ("soc/tegra: Use ARM SMCCC to get chip ID, revision, and platform info")
Signed-off-by: Alexander Schwankner <mrmoor4@googlemail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/tegra/fuse/tegra-apbmisc.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/tegra/fuse/tegra-apbmisc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/tegra/fuse/tegra-apbmisc.c
@@ -78,15 +78,35 @@
 		return TEGRA_SMCCC_MINOR_REV(revision);
 #endif
 	return (tegra_read_chipid() >> 16) & 0xf;
+
+}
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_SMCCC_DISCOVERY)
+/*
+ * The TF-A firmware on these SoCs implements the SMCCC SoC ID call, but it
+ * reports the major revision in bits [15:8] of the SoC revision rather than
+ * the platform. Their platform has to be read from HIDREV instead.
+ */
+static bool tegra_smccc_has_platform(void)
+{
+	switch (tegra_get_chip_id()) {
+	case TEGRA210:
+	case TEGRA186:
+	case TEGRA194:
+	case TEGRA234:
+		return false;
+	}
 
+	return true;
 }
+#endif
 
 u8 tegra_get_platform(void)
 {
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_SMCCC_DISCOVERY)
 	s32 revision = arm_smccc_get_soc_id_revision();
 
-	if (revision >= 0)
+	if (revision >= 0 && tegra_smccc_has_platform())
 		return TEGRA_SMCCC_PLATFORM(revision);
 #endif
 	return (tegra_read_chipid() >> 20) & 0xf;
-- 
2.51.0
